# The family repos live inside this dir but are their own git repos.
#
# ⚠️ Two of these are one dot apart: `haus/` is the PLATFORM checkout
# (`hausfold/haus`, renamed there 2026-08-11) and `hausfold.co/` is the SITE
# (`hausfold/hausfold.co`, not in FAMILY). Two different repos; each directory
# is named for its own. A pre-rename spelling reappearing here means something
# re-cloned the layer under a name `bench` will not find.
/haus/
/hausfold.co/
/homebrew-tap/
/holt/
/nebelung/
/pounce/
/perch/
/org-profile/
/trill/
# `ops` is PRIVATE and not in FAMILY — no flake edge, nothing to build — but it
# IS in DOCS_REPOS and in `bench clone`, because the docs sweep reconciles its
# files like any other repo's. Without this line the clone leaves `?? ops/` here
# and a `git add -A` up top tries to add a nested repo. That is the trap #283
# left behind with `messages/`; don't wait for it.
/ops/
.DS_Store

# Coverage dumps. An LLVM-instrumented binary writes `default.profraw` into
# whatever directory it was *run* from, not where it was built — so one stray
# family tool on PATH leaves one HERE, in whatever tree the shell was sitting
# in, and `holt` reads it as unlanded work. perch was that tool; its Xcode
# project pins `ENABLE_CODE_COVERAGE = NO` now, which is the actual fix. This
# line only covers the workshop's own tree — every child repo is wholly
# ignored above, so it can't reach inside one; `perch` and `trill` carry their
# own, `haus`, `holt`, `nebelung` and `pounce` don't yet.
*.profraw
